/target/
# This is a library crate, not a binary: Cargo.lock is deliberately not committed (the standard
# convention for libraries: a consuming binary resolves its own dependency versions; committing
# ours here would only pin them for this crate's own `cargo test`/`cargo build` runs, which is
# what CI regenerating it from Cargo.toml on every run already covers just as well).
/Cargo.lock
